# The secrets this blog takes. Copy this file to `.dev.vars` to use them locally
# (`.dev.vars` stays out of git).
#
# **This file is also what the Deploy to Cloudflare screen reads.** Deploying from the
# button turns every key in here into a field to fill in, and what you type becomes a
# Worker secret.
#
# Leave them empty locally and the admin UI still opens: lily falls back to the
# `localhostOnly` adapter, which only passes when the host is localhost or 127.0.0.1,
# and therefore never passes on a real domain.

# The admin password. **Use 12 characters or more.**
#
# Anything shorter is refused outright — the only defence against brute force here is a
# delay on failure, so a short password would be protected by nothing. **Nothing checks
# this while you type**: the deploy screen takes whatever you give it, and the admin UI
# then refuses to open. Getting out of that means replacing the secret **and deploying
# again** — saving it alone leaves the running Worker on the old value.
#
# Replacing it also voids every login cookie already handed out.
ADMIN_PASSWORD=

# Announcing posts on Bluesky (optional). **Used only when both are set**; with either
# missing, the announce button in the admin UI says "not configured" and nothing else
# changes. Use an App Password, not your account password.
# BLUESKY_IDENTIFIER=
# BLUESKY_APP_PASSWORD=
